{"orgCode":"0985","name":"California School Finance Authority","agencyCode":"0010","agencyName":"Legislative, Judicial, and Executive","description":"The California School Finance Authority (CSFA), created in 1985, provides facilities and working capital financing to school districts, community college districts, county offices of education, and charter schools. The State Treasurer serves as chair of CSFA, and the Superintendent of Public Instruction and the Director of Finance serve as members. CSFA has offices in Los Angeles and Sacramento.\n\nCSFA serves as the primary state agency for California nonprofit charter schools seeking facility and working capital funding through several state and federal programs.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":189413,"cy":204822,"by":206734},"positions":{"py":13.8,"cy":17,"by":17},"excluded":{"nongovernmental":{"py":1894,"cy":13105,"by":12985}}},"programs":{"id":"exp/0010/0985","kind":"department","name":"California School Finance Authority","code":"0985","amounts":{"py":189413,"cy":204822,"by":206734},"positions":{"py":13.8,"cy":17,"by":17},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":169172,"cy":182885,"by":184788},"bond":{"py":574,"cy":1412,"by":1412},"federal":{"py":19667,"cy":20525,"by":20534}},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0985/0920","kind":"program","name":"Charter School Facilities Program","code":"0920","amounts":{"py":574,"cy":1412,"by":1412},"byFundType":{"bond":{"py":574,"cy":1412,"by":1412}},"positions":{"py":3.8,"cy":5,"by":5},"description":"0920 - CHARTER SCHOOL FACILITIES PROGRAM\n\nChapter 935, Statutes of 2002, as amended by Chapter 587, Statutes of 2003, created the Charter School Facilities Program (CSFP), which provides funding for the new construction, renovation or rehabilitation of charter school facilities. CSFA and the Office of Public School Construction jointly administer the program. CSFP was funded through the Kindergarten-University Public Education Facilities Bond Acts of 2002, 2004, 2006, 2016, and 2024 for a total of $2 billion. The program provides a 50 percent state subsidy for charter school facilities project costs, with the balance of the project costs being repaid (to the state) by the charter school through a 30-year loan. Recipient charter schools must provide site-based instruction, be financially sound, and meet other program eligibility requirements.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":574,"cy":1869,"by":1749}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0985/0920/f6044","kind":"fund","name":"2004 State School Facilities Fund","code":"6044","amounts":{"py":49,"cy":0,"by":0},"byFundType":{"bond":{"py":49,"cy":0,"by":0}},"extra":{"fundType":"bond","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":49,"cy":0,"by":0}}}},{"id":"exp/0010/0985/0920/f6057","kind":"fund","name":"2006 State School Facilities Fund","code":"6057","amounts":{"py":525,"cy":1412,"by":1412},"byFundType":{"bond":{"py":525,"cy":1412,"by":1412}},"extra":{"fundType":"bond","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":525,"cy":1412,"by":1412}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/0010/0985/0920/f9735","kind":"fund","name":"2006 Charter School Facilities Account, 2006 State School Facilities Fund","code":"9735","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":457,"by":337},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":0,"cy":457,"by":337}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":457,"by":337}}}}],"excluded":{"nongovernmental":{"py":0,"cy":457,"by":337}}},{"id":"exp/0010/0985/0925","kind":"program","name":"State Charter School Facilities Incentive Grants Program","code":"0925","amounts":{"py":19667,"cy":20525,"by":20534},"byFundType":{"federal":{"py":19667,"cy":20525,"by":20534}},"positions":{"py":1,"cy":3,"by":3},"description":"0925 - STATE CHARTER SCHOOL FACILITIES INCENTIVE GRANTS PROGRAM\n\nIn 2004, 2009, 2014, and 2024, CSFA received grants under the United States Department of Education's State Charter School Facilities Incentive Grants Program (Assistance Listing Number 84.282D) to provide California charter schools with assistance for facilities costs. Grant funds reimburse a charter school's costs for rent, lease, mortgage or debt service payments for existing or new facilities or the costs of acquiring land and/or constructing or renovating a facility. Grants are awarded to charter schools based on preference points assigned based on the percentage of low-income students, percentage of overcrowding, not-for-profit status, and demonstrated student performance. Schools cannot use program funds to supplant state funding.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":167,"cy":525,"by":534},"Local Assistance":{"py":19500,"cy":20000,"by":20000}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0985/0925/f0890","kind":"fund","name":"Federal Trust Fund","code":"0890","amounts":{"py":19667,"cy":20525,"by":20534},"byFundType":{"federal":{"py":19667,"cy":20525,"by":20534}},"extra":{"fundType":"federal","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":167,"cy":525,"by":534},"Local Assistance":{"py":19500,"cy":20000,"by":20000}}}}]},{"id":"exp/0010/0985/0930","kind":"program","name":"Charter School Facility Grant Program","code":"0930","amounts":{"py":169019,"cy":182727,"by":184630},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":169019,"cy":182727,"by":184630}},"positions":{"py":6,"cy":6,"by":6},"description":"0930 - CHARTER SCHOOL FACILITY GRANT PROGRAM\n\nThe Charter School Facility Grant Program provides Proposition 98 General Fund grants to assist charter schools with rent and lease costs. This program targets schools and communities with significant populations of economically disadvantaged students. Eligible charter schools are provided the lesser of: 75 percent of annual eligible facilities rent and lease costs; or a rate per unit of classroom-based average daily attendance annually adjusted by a statutory cost-of-living adjustment.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":978,"cy":994,"by":993},"Local Assistance":{"py":168041,"cy":181733,"by":183637}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0985/0930/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":169019,"cy":182727,"by":184630},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":169019,"cy":182727,"by":184630}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":978,"cy":994,"by":993},"Local Assistance":{"py":168041,"cy":181733,"by":183637}}}}]},{"id":"exp/0010/0985/0935","kind":"program","name":"Charter School Revolving Loan Program","code":"0935","amounts":{"py":153,"cy":158,"by":158},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":153,"cy":158,"by":158}},"positions":{"py":1,"cy":1,"by":1},"description":"0935 - CHARTER SCHOOL REVOLVING LOAN FUND\n\nCharter 1010, Statutes of 1976 established the Charter School Revolving Loan Fund in the State Treasury to provide loans of up to $250,000 to new charter schools to assist them in meeting the purposes of the school's approved charter. The program is available to any charter school that is not a conversion of an existing public school, and preference goes to schools that have not opened nor completed their full charter term. Chapter 776, Statutes of 2025 amended the program, including by increasing the total lifetime loan amount to $500,000 and prioritizing loans for disaster impacted schools.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":153,"cy":158,"by":158},"Local Assistance":{"py":1100,"cy":12386,"by":12386}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0985/0935/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":153,"cy":158,"by":158},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":153,"cy":158,"by":158}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":153,"cy":158,"by":158}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/0010/0985/0935/f0606","kind":"fund","name":"Charter School Revolving Loan Fund","code":"0606","amounts":{"py":1100,"cy":12386,"by":12386},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":1100,"cy":12386,"by":12386}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":1100,"cy":12386,"by":12386}}}}],"excluded":{"nongovernmental":{"py":1100,"cy":12386,"by":12386}}}],"sources":[{"label":"ebudget.ca.gov API: orgProgram/0985","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/api/budget/e/2026-27/orgProgram/0985"},{"label":"Detailed Expenditures by Program (PDF)","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/2026-27/pdf/Enacted/GovernorsBudget/0010/0985.pdf"}],"extra":{"legalCitations":"PROGRAM AUTHORITY\n\nEducation Code Sections 17078.52-17078.66, 17170-17199.6, 41365, 41366.5, 41366.7, 41367, and 47614.5"},"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/0010/0985/0918","kind":"program","name":"Smart Bonds","code":"0918","amounts":{"py":794,"cy":262,"by":262},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":794,"cy":262,"by":262}},"positions":{"py":2,"cy":2,"by":2},"description":"0918 - SMART BONDS PROGRAM\n\nChapter 1438, Statutes of 1985, as amended by Chapter 598, Statutes of 1987, established CSFA and authorized the issuance of revenue bonds or other debt instruments. The proceeds from the sale of the bonds are available for loans to schools and community college districts to assist with the acquisition of equipment and new school sites, construction of new facilities, reconstruction of existing facilities, capital improvements, and providing working capital. Chapter 325, Statutes of 2006 (AB 2717), allows CSFA to issue debt on behalf of California charter schools for capital improvements and working capital needs.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":794,"cy":262,"by":262}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0985/0918/f0526","kind":"fund","name":"California School Finance Authority Fund","code":"0526","amounts":{"py":794,"cy":262,"by":262},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":794,"cy":262,"by":262}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":794,"cy":262,"by":262}}}}]}],"excluded":{"nongovernmental":{"py":1894,